<%# Turbo Stream response for POST /calculators/:slug (issue #31). The controller
    renders this for BOTH branches with @calc set:
      • success → default render of this template (calc.valid?)
      • invalid → render "calculators/create", status: :unprocessable_entity
    so this one template covers both states by handing @calc to _result, which
    decides answer-vs-errors. It replaces the #result target in place, leaving the
    input form (and the visitor's entries) untouched — the progressive-enhancement
    payoff over a full-page reload. %>
<%= turbo_stream.replace "result" do %>
  <%= render "calculators/result", calc: @calc %>
<% end %>
